※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4460

※ Which member is wanted decides what type the expression has, so it has to be
※ known while compiling.  A name bound inside a function is not: what it stands
※ for is the value an expression produced, and whether that expression could
※ have been worked out while compiling is a question about the expression rather
※ than about the name.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let p: 〈u8, u8〉 = 〈1u8, 2u8〉
    let at: u8 = 1u8
    p⟦at⟧
